nto the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-6{x}_{1}+6(\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{3})+9{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the steady-state vector must be stochastic, its entries should add up to $1.$ Therefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3}+\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{11}{2}{x}_{3} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{2}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nq=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{11} \\\\ \\frac{3}{11} \\\\ \\frac{2}{11}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b-c=\\frac{6}{11}+\\frac{3}{11}-\\frac{2}{11}=\\frac{7}{11}.\n$$" 13194139535294 true] [17592186342274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342275 13194139535294 true] [17592186342274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342276 13194139535294 true] [17592186342274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342277 13194139535294 true] [17592186342274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342278 13194139535294 true] [17592186342274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342279 13194139535294 true] [17592186342274 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535294 true] [17592186342274 1041 "selection" 13194139535294 true] [17592186342274 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342278 13194139535294 true] [17592186342274 1110 #uuid "8c26d446-a25a-5bf8-9909-7a8bf199311f" 13194139535294 true] [17592186342275 1034 "\\frac{11}{25}" 13194139535294 true] [17592186342275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535294 true] [17592186342275 1111 #uuid "bed4e822-8907-5378-98ee-1e5f188dfd74" 13194139535294 true] [17592186342276 1034 "\\frac{13}{21}" 13194139535294 true] [17592186342276 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535294 true] [17592186342276 1111 #uuid "a281f01a-da97-51f6-8eed-270aac899700" 13194139535294 true] [17592186342277 1034 "\\frac{3}{5}" 13194139535294 true] [17592186342277 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535294 true] [17592186342277 1111 #uuid "4e5b2ab7-0f38-555f-8755-3a8b4ce94fb4" 13194139